 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 666813,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">range()</code> function can also be used to iterate a list-of-lists. Which code prints each number in <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">my_list</code> starting from <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">7</code>, then <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">4</code>, and so on, ending with <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">-5</code>, using counting <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for</code> loops?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1329452,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for column_index in range(0, len(my_list[0])):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;for row_index in range (0, len(my_list)):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(my_list[row_index][column_index])\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The outer for loop runs for 4 iterations. The inner for loop runs for 3 iterations. But numbers are printed in a different order."
    },
    {
     "id": 1329453,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for row_index in range(0, len(my_list)):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;for column_index in range (0, len(my_list)):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(my_list[row_index][column_index])\n&nbsp;&nbsp;print()\n</pre>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The outer for loop runs for 3 iterations because there are 3 elements in the list-of-lists. The inner for loop runs for 3 iterations, but each row actually has 4 elements. Thus, the numbers 12, 16, and -5 will not be printed. "
    },
    {
     "id": 1329454,
     "content_html": "<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for row_index in range(0, len(my_list)):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;for column_index in range (0, len(my_list[0])):\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(my_list[row_index][column_index])\n</pre>\n",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "The outer <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for</code> loop runs for three iterations because there are three elements in the list-of-lists. The inner <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">for</code> loop iterates through each element of each row using the length of each row."
    }
   ],
